# downstream reliances — the JUDGED ask channel (the tenth ask: open text stops
# feeding the rules). One line per upstream LAW a consumer stands on:
#
#     <theory> | <equation, exactly as the lock renders it>: <consumer> — <why>
#
# Judged on every test run by `Dependence::judge_register` (the self-judgment form:
# the committed lock on both sides), so a re-bless that drops a relied-on law refuses
# BY NAME — equation, consumer, why — before the release ships. A stale entry is a
# lie to delete; the justification is the ratification.
#
# SURFACE (API) reliances are the compiler's to judge instead: one line each in
# `downstream-fixture/tests/reliances.rs`.
#
# Consumers author their own lines by PR. Empty today is honest: the surface exists;
# no law reliance has been declared through it yet.
